#
# System properties for y2q (Galaxy S20+ 5G, SM-G9860, SM8250)
#

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IMS bring-up overrides
#
# These force the telephony framework to advertise VoLTE / VT / VoWiFi as
# available regardless of what the carrier reports.  They exist so that the
# UI toggles and ImsResolver come up while bringing the userspace IMS stack
# (packages/apps/PhhIms) online, and are NOT a substitute for correct
# CarrierConfig - see overlay/packages/apps/CarrierConfig/res/xml/vendor.xml.
#
# They MUST be written as integers: system/sepolicy/private/property_contexts
# labels persist.dbg.{volte,vt,wfc}_avail_ovr as "exact int", so a value of
# "true" is rejected by init and the override silently does nothing.
#
# Only the three properties that actually exist in AOSP are set.  The upstream
# PhhIms README also suggests persist.dbg.allow_ims_off, but there is no such
# property anywhere in this tree's property_contexts (a grep for persist.dbg
# returns exactly the twelve volte/vt/wfc *_ovr entries), so it is omitted
# rather than shipped as dead config.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
persist.dbg.volte_avail_ovr=1
persist.dbg.vt_avail_ovr=0
persist.dbg.wfc_avail_ovr=1
